---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import ArrowLink from '../components/ArrowLink.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import PendingCopy from '../components/PendingCopy.astro';
import { MEDIA } from '../content/media';
import { SITE } from '../content/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Pierce O’Brien | Pierce O’Brien Piano"
  description="Meet Pierce O’Brien and learn about the careful listening, assessment, and plain-language guidance behind his piano work."
>
  <PageIntro
    title="About Pierce"
    introduction="Pierce O’Brien is the named technician behind every appointment—a careful listener who treats tuning as part of a larger relationship between the piano, the player, and the room."
    image={MEDIA.portrait}
    imageAlt="Portrait of Pierce O’Brien seated in front of a grand piano"
    imagePosition="center 28%"
    actionLabel="Book With Pierce"
  />

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="portrait-layout shell">
      <div class="media-frame">
        <Image
          src={MEDIA.workingMonochrome}
          alt="Pierce O’Brien working at the open strings of a grand piano"
          widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 40vw"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>A career that began with one piano.</h2>
        <p>
          Pierce’s path into piano technology began when a choir member gave him a baby grand. He
          refurbished and reconditioned the instrument, learned the fundamentals of tuning, and used
          that experience as a starting point for deeper study and a career in piano care.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today, the work is still grounded in the same instinct: listen closely, understand the
          instrument in front of you, and explain what matters without making the owner feel out of
          their depth.
        </p>
        <p>
          Aural listening remains central to Pierce’s approach. Tuning is the most familiar piano
          service, but it belongs in a larger conversation about the instrument’s pitch, touch,
          tonal character, and mechanical response.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is why regulation and voicing are considered alongside tuning when they are relevant:
          each service addresses a different part of the playing experience, and the right next step
          starts with the piano in front of you.
        </p>
        <PendingCopy>
          Exact apprenticeship, experience, and service-count wording requires final owner
          verification before it appears here.
        </PendingCopy>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Quiet confidence, visible in the process.</h2>
        <p>
          Quality is communicated through assessment, careful work, honest limits, and useful next
          steps—not comparison or hype.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="process-rail">
        <section class="process-step">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Precise</h3>
          <p>Specific about what is being heard, assessed, and addressed.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="process-step">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Observant</h3>
          <p>Attentive to pitch, touch, tone, condition, and the player’s goals.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="process-step">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Approachable</h3>
          <p>Plain language and respect for any piano that matters to its owner.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="owner-event shell">
      <div class="owner-event-copy">
        <h2>A record of continued study.</h2>
        <p>
          This owner-supplied photograph records Pierce at the 2026 Piano Technicians Guild
          convention. Exact public credential wording remains absent from the site facts and copy
          until the owner approves it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="owner-event-photo">
        <Image
          src={MEDIA.rptEvent}
          alt="Pierce O’Brien beside an event display at a piano-technician convention"
          widths={[420, 720, 1080, 1400]}
          sizes="(max-width: 960px) 86vw, 42vw"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>Owner-supplied convention photograph.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark statement">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="statement-copy">
        The value of a piano is not limited to its price. A family’s first upright deserves the same
        honest attention as a performance grand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="closing-action shell">
      <h2>Work directly with the technician.</h2>
      <ArrowLink href={SITE.booking.internalPath} label="Book Now" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
